From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NotAlexNoyle <alexnoyle@icloud.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 10:25:54 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] gpu compositor spike: an in-process OpenGL compositor behind
 the offscreen widget (JIHAD_GPU_COMPOSITOR)

With JIHAD_GPU_COMPOSITOR in the environment (and JIHAD_DISABLE_OMTC
unset) the offscreen PuppetWidget creates an in-process compositor
through nsBaseWidget::CreateCompositor behind a ClientLayerManager;
gfxPlatformHeadless lists LAYERS_OPENGL when hardware compositing is
enabled, and the env counts as layers.acceleration.force-enabled in
gfxPlatform (AccelerateLayersByDefault() is false without
MOZ_GL_PROVIDER, the headless GfxInfo answers UNKNOWN). The new export
jihad_offscreen_compose paints the document as layers (PresShell::Paint
on the root view) and fetches the composited frame over the upstream
snapshot road (BeginTransactionWithTarget + EndEmptyTransaction ->
SendMakeSnapshot -> ForceComposeToTarget -> glReadPixels), logging the
two timings per frame. Without the env nothing changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01J67ZH8aYy8uzhgZDZ6Nvx9
